            "id": "msg_040bae270a",
            "role": "user",
            "content": "# Full Repository Architecture Analysis \u2013 Staff Authentication & Patient Registration (No Code Changes)\n\nPerform a complete end-to-end analysis of the entire repository.\n\nDo NOT modify any code.\n\nThe goal is to understand every connection between the React frontend, PHP backend, and MySQL database (phpMyAdmin).\n\nProduce a comprehensive architecture document with diagrams, file names, function names, API endpoints, SQL tables, and execution flow.\n\n---\n\n# Part 1 \u2013 Staff Registration\n\nTrace the entire registration flow.\n\nStart from:\n\n* React page\n* Form component\n* Hook\n* Service\n* API client\n* PHP endpoint\n* Validation\n* SQL query\n* MySQL tables\n* Audit logging\n* Response\n* Frontend state update\n\nFor every step include:\n\n* filename\n* function\n* line number\n* input\n* output\n* validation\n* errors\n* SQL executed\n\nExplain exactly what is inserted into MySQL.\n\nIdentify every table involved.\n\n---\n\n# Part 2 \u2013 Staff Login\n\nTrace the complete login process.\n\nFrom:\n\nLogin Form\n\n\u2193\n\nReact Component\n\n\u2193\n\nHook\n\n\u2193\n\nService\n\n\u2193\n\nPHP API\n\n\u2193\n\nPassword verification\n\n\u2193\n\nSession creation\n\n\u2193\n\nCookie creation\n\n\u2193\n\nuser_sessions table\n\n\u2193\n\nReact Context\n\n\u2193\n\nProtected Routes\n\nInclude:\n\n* every file\n* every function\n* every API call\n* every middleware\n* every SQL query\n* every cookie\n* every session check\n\nExplain how phpMyAdmin reflects every stage.\n\n---\n\n# Part 3 \u2013 Admin Approval\n\nTrace:\n\nPending registration\n\n\u2193\n\nApproval\n\n\u2193\n\nRole assignment\n\n\u2193\n\nDatabase updates\n\n\u2193\n\nAudit logs\n\n\u2193\n\nLogin eligibility\n\nShow every table modified.\n\n---\n\n# Part 4 \u2013 Staff Profile\n\nTrace:\n\nProfile page\n\n\u2193\n\nUpdate profile\n\n\u2193\n\nUpload photo\n\n\u2193\n\nSignature\n\n\u2193\n\nSpecialization\n\n\u2193\n\nPhone\n\n\u2193\n\nBMDC\n\n\u2193\n\nDatabase update\n\nExplain exactly which table and columns are updated.\n\n---\n\n# Part 5 \u2013 Patient Registration\n\nTrace the complete patient registration process.\n\nInclude:\n\nReception\n\n\u2193\n\nEmergency\n\n\u2193\n\nOnline registration\n\n\u2193\n\nAppointment booking\n\n\u2193\n\nWalk-in\n\n\u2193\n\nAdmission\n\n\u2193\n\nPatient creation\n\n\u2193\n\nDatabase\n\nIdentify:\n\n* every component\n* every hook\n* every service\n* every API\n* every SQL query\n\nShow all database tables.\n\nExplain relationships.\n\n---\n\n# Part 6 \u2013 Patient Login\n\nTrace:\n\nPatient registration\n\n\u2193\n\nApproval\n\n\u2193\n\nLogin\n\n\u2193\n\nSession creation\n\n\u2193\n\nCookie\n\n\u2193\n\nAuthentication\n\n\u2193\n\nDashboard\n\n\u2193\n\nLogout\n\nShow every PHP endpoint and SQL query.\n\n---\n\n# Part 7 \u2013 Database Analysis\n\nAnalyse every authentication-related table.\n\nInclude:\n\nusers\n\nuser_sessions\n\nadmin_accounts\n\npatient_login\n\npatient_sessions\n\npatients\n\nstaff\n\naudit_logs\n\nsettings\n\nFor each table provide:\n\n* purpose\n* primary key\n* foreign keys\n* relationships\n* indexes\n* columns\n* where it is used\n\nExplain how phpMyAdmin represents these relationships.\n\n---\n\n# Part 8 \u2013 API Mapping\n\nCreate a table:\n\nFrontend Component\n\n\u2193\n\nHook\n\n\u2193\n\nService\n\n\u2193\n\nAPI Endpoint\n\n\u2193\n\nPHP File\n\n\u2193\n\nDatabase Table\n\n\u2193\n\nSQL Operation\n\nCover:\n\n* Authentication\n* Staff\n* Patients\n* Visits\n* Admissions\n* Prescriptions\n* Appointments\n* Payments\n* Notifications\n* Settings\n* Landing Page\n\n---\n\n# Part 9 \u2013 Session Architecture\n\nExplain:\n\n* PHP Session lifecycle\n* session_token creation\n* user_sessions usage\n* cookie configuration\n* session verification\n* logout\n* expiry\n* restore after refresh\n\nDraw the complete flow.\n\n---\n\n# Part 10 \u2013 phpMyAdmin Mapping\n\nFor every user action explain exactly what changes inside MySQL.\n\nExamples:\n\nStaff Registration\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT users\n\n\u2193\n\nAudit log\n\n\u2193\n\nPending approval\n\nPatient Registration\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT patients\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT patient_login\n\n\u2193\n\nAudit log\n\nAppointment Booking\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT appointments\n\nPrescription\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT prescriptions\n\nVisit\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT visits\n\nPayment\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT payments\n\nAdmission\n\n\u2193\n\nINSERT admissions\n\nBed Assignment\n\n\u2193\n\nUPDATE beds\n\nShow every SQL operation.\n\n---\n\n# Part 11 \u2013 Data Flow Diagram\n\nCreate a complete architecture diagram:\n\nBrowser\n\n\u2193\n\nReact Components\n\n\u2193\n\nHooks\n\n\u2193\n\nServices\n\n\u2193\n\nAPI Client\n\n\u2193\n\nPHP API\n\n\u2193\n\nMiddleware\n\n\u2193\n\nAuthentication\n\n\u2193\n\nPDO\n\n\u2193\n\nMySQL\n\n\u2193\n\nphpMyAdmin\n\nInclude all major modules.\n\n---\n\n# Part 12 \u2013 Dependency Graph\n\nGenerate a dependency graph showing:\n\nReact Component\n\n\u2193\n\nHook\n\n\u2193\n\nService\n\n\u2193\n\nPHP Endpoint\n\n\u2193\n\nDatabase Table\n\nfor all authentication and patient-related features.\n\n---\n\n# Part 13 \u2013 Findings\n\nIdentify:\n\n* duplicate logic\n* dead code\n* unreachable APIs\n* missing endpoints\n* missing foreign keys\n* inconsistent naming\n* security concerns\n* performance bottlenecks\n* redundant SQL\n* race conditions\n* transaction issues\n\nDo not modify code.\n\nOnly analyse.\n\nSupport every finding with evidence (file names, functions, and line numbers).\n\nThe final report should be detailed enough that a new developer can understand exactly how staff login, patient registration, authentication, sessions, and phpMyAdmin interact throughout the entire application.",
